Concrete Rhino REST API Specification
Oct 20, 2026 · @Chris Kranich
Automation Logic, LLC publishes this specification for third-party software developers
who interface with the Concrete Rhino Automated Batching System.
1. Purpose
This specification defines the REST API that third-party software uses to exchange data
with a Concrete Rhino Automated Batching System. Dispatch, office and quality-control
software can use it to send orders, tickets, customers, mix designs and material settings
to a plant, and to read back its orders, loads and batch results.
It is written for software developers building that interface. It describes every resource,
field, rule and reply the plant supports; anything it doesn't describe is not supported.
2. Relationship to BCQCI
The API is a branch of BCQCI, the Interface Specification Between Concrete
Batching/Dispatching Software and Quality Control/Mix Design Software developed with
Stonemont Solutions (version 3.4, November 2017).
