Concrete Rhino REST API Specification
Page 5 of 35

-- 5 of 35 --

Dates in a URL are YYYY-MM-DD . Any code shaped like NNNN-NN-NN is read as a date, so
don't use order numbers of that form. Under orders another code is an order number;
under loads and batchresults it must be a ticket number, a whole number above 0, or
the reply is 400. A date range covers whole days; a start after the end returns 400, and
orders/<from>/<to> allows at most 93 days. orderstatus/ and orderloads/ need an
order number (400 without one).
A trailing slash is fine: orders and orders/ are the same.
Query strings ( ?name=value ) are passed through, but no resource uses them yet.
Codes with special characters must be URL-encoded: D & M is D%20%26%20M . A plus sign
must be sent as %2B; a bare + is read as a space. A code that contains / can't be used in
a URL even when encoded. Use the body's code field instead (section 16).
Short forms ( …list ) return the same records with fewer fields, each wrapped in
listitem instead of the record's own name.
6. Responses
Every response starts with a request_status block. Check request_status.status ,
not the HTTP status line, which is always 200.
{
"request_status": { "status": 400, "msg": "BAD REQUEST", "detail": "Unknown
mix_code." },
"error_detail": "Order 445676: mix 3000XX not found."
}
URL 	Method What it does
batchresultlist/… 	GET 	Same as batchresults , short
form
batchresults/since/<result_id> 	GET 	Results finished after that result
id; batchresultlist/since/…
for the short form
status/ or status/<result_id> 	GET 	Ping: plant identity, clock,
versions, newest result id and
results pending
