7. Data rules
A PUT changes only the fields it sends; every field it leaves out keeps its stored value.
Sent with a value: the stored value is replaced.
Sent as "" : a text field is blanked. A blank code ( cust_code , mix_code , order_num , a
plant code) counts as not sent.
Not sent: nothing changes. On a new record the field gets its default.
Request body. A PUT or POST body is an array named for the resource, with each record
wrapped in its singular name: {"orders": [{"order": {...}}, {"order": {...}}]} .
One request can carry many records, except when the URL names a code: then the array
must hold exactly one.
status msg 	detail 	When
409 	CONFLICT 	Conflicts with what is
stored.
A code deleted at the plant; a
code another product already
uses; a material sent with a
different type; a customer
name already in use; a ticket
that has started batching or
was canceled, a ticket for a
canceled order, a ticket
number still open on another
order, a truck deleted at the
plant; a mix being batched, or a
mix component sent as a
different type
409 	CONFLICT 	Database Error. 	The database refused the
write
501 	NOT
IMPLEMENTED
(none) 	Any other HTTP method
503 	SERVICE
UNAVAILABLE
Database is busy. 	The plant database is busy; try
again
Concrete Rhino REST API Specification
Page 9 of 35

-- 9 of 35 --

All or nothing. The plant checks every record before it writes any. If one is rejected,
nothing in the request is saved and error_detail names the record ("Record 3: ...", or the
code when the URL names one, such as "Ticket 100050: ..."). Records that pass are written
together in one transaction. Plants are the exception (section 8).
Which record. When the URL names a code, that code picks the record and the body's
code may rename it. Without one, the body's code picks the record.
Numbers may be sent as JSON numbers or as strings: 5 , 5.0 and "5" are the same.
true and false count as 1 and 0, and null or "" counts as not sent. A string that isn't a
number is rejected with error_detail naming the field. Whole-number fields accept
5.0 but not 5.5 .
Dates in a body may be YYYY-MM-DD , MM-DD-YYYY or MM/DD/YYYY , with or without
leading zeros, for years 2000 to 2099. The plant can't tell a day-first date from a month-
first one: 05-03-2026 is read as May 3, and only a day above 12 ( 19-03-2026 ) is refused.
Send YYYY-MM-DD to be safe. Responses always use YYYY-MM-DD .
Times may be H:MM , HH:MM or HH:MM:SS , 24-hour, and nothing else: 8:00 PM and 8:5
are refused. They are stored to the minute.
Text length. Text longer than a field holds is cut to fit, except codes that pick a record
( order_num , mix_code , mc_code , truck_num , driver_name ), which are refused with
400. Limits are given with each resource.
Responses send some numbers as strings (for example "mat_dosagetype": "0" ). Read
every field so that either form works.
8. Plants
Each plant computer has one plant code of its own (for example 101 ). Every
mat_plantcode , cust_plantcode and order plant_code you send is checked against it.
Field 	Type 	Notes
plant_code 	text, up to 7 	Required on PUT/POST; a code in the URL counts.
Matched without regard to case
plant_name 	text, up to 47
plant_address text, up to 95
Concrete Rhino REST API Specification
Page 10 of 35

-- 10 of 35 --

GET plants/ returns every plant record stored on this computer, except deleted ones:
{ "request_status": {...}, "plants": [ { "plant": { "plant_code": "101",
"plant_name": "Kenai, AK", "plant_address": "Kenai, AK" } } ] }
GET plants/<code> returns this computer's own plant as a single "plant": {...}
object, whatever code is given.
PUT or POST plants/ adds a plant record, or with PUT updates the one with the same
plant_code ; POST of an existing plant returns 409. PUT plants/<code> updates the
plant with that code, and a different plant_code in the body renames it; without one, the
code stays. An unknown code returns 404 Unsupported resource.
Plants work differently from the other resources:
A field left out is blanked, not kept (except the code, above).
Records are written one at a time, in order, without a transaction. The first record that
fails stops the request; records before it stay saved, and error_detail says so.
Changing the code of this computer's own plant changes the plant code every other
request is checked against.
9. Customers
PUT creates a customer that doesn't exist and updates one that does. POST only creates.
Customer codes match exactly but without regard to case: cash finds Cash . A customer
deleted at the plant isn't returned by GET, and a PUT or POST of its code returns 409
Conflicts with what is stored. The same customer twice in one request is refused
(400).
Field 	GET 	PUT/POST 	Notes
cust_code 	yes 	required 	Up to 15 characters. Optional in
the body when the URL names
the customer
cust_name 	yes 	required for a
new customer
Up to 64. No two customers
may have the same name,
matched with case (409)
