GET customers/ returns "customers": [{"customer": {...}}] , ordered by credit
type, then code. GET customers/<code> returns one "customer": {...} . GET
customerlist/ returns "customerlist": [{"listitem": {"cust_code": ...,
"cust_name": ...}}] .
New customers start as COD, price tier 1, no discount and not tax exempt. Discount and
tax-exempt status can't be set through the API, and a PUT never changes them.
Rename: PUT customers/Cash with "cust_code": "CASH2" in the body renames the
customer. A rename onto a code that's already in use returns 409, and a rename that
changes only the case of the code is ignored. When the customer in the URL doesn't exist,
the body's code must match the URL's (400 otherwise).
