PUT /rhino_rest_api/v1/json/customers/
{ "customers": [ { "customer": {
"cust_code": "JF100", "cust_name": "Johnson Flatwork",
"cust_first_name": "Mike", "cust_last_name": "Johnson",
"cust_address": "3211 Providence Dr, Anchorage, AK 99508",
"cust_phone": "907-555-0100", "cust_udf1": 1 } } ] }
Open question: cust_udf2 reads back the discount but is written as the price tier. A
client that reads a customer and sends it back may get a 400 (a discount outside 1–3) or
set the wrong tier. Until this is settled, don't send cust_udf2 .
10. Materials
Materials can be read and updated but not created: each one is tied to a bin and its plant
wiring. A PUT or POST for an unknown material returns 404, and a POST for a known one
returns 409, so POST never succeeds. Material codes are case-sensitive, unlike customer
and mix codes.
Field 	GET 	PUT 	Notes
mat_code 	yes 	required 	Up to 19 characters. Optional
in the body when the URL
names the material; then a
different code renames it. A
code another product already
uses returns 409
mat_name 	yes 	ignored 	Same as mat_code
mat_plantcode 	yes 	optional 	If sent, must be this plant's
code (403 otherwise)
mat_type 	yes 	optional 	Type code (table below). It
must be in the stored type's
family; another family or an
unknown code returns 409
mat_source 	yes 	yes 	Up to 9 characters
mat_spgr 	yes 	yes 	Specific gravity, more than 0
and at most 10
