11. Mixes
Mixes can be read, created and changed. A PUT or POST takes the same shape GET
returns, so a mix can be read, edited and sent back (section 11.1).
GET mixdesigns/ returns every mix, and GET mixdesigns/<mix_code> returns one as a
single "mixdesign" object. The list form looks like this:
{ "request_status": {...},
"mixdesigns": [ { "mixdesign": {
"mixinfo": { "mix_plantcode": "101", "mix_code": "3000INT", ... },
"mixcomponents": [ { "mixcomponent": { "mc_code": "Cem1", ... } } ] } }
] }
GET mixdesignlist/ returns "mixdesignlist": [{"listitem": {"mix_code",
"mix_name"}}] .
mixinfo field 	Meaning
mix_plantcode This plant's code
mix_code 	Mix code, up to 19 characters
mix_name 	Description
mix_unittype 	0 US (yd³), 1 metric (m³)
mix_maxsize 	Largest load
mix_slump 	Slump
mix_price 	Price per unit
mix_mixtime 	Mixing time, minutes
mix_air 	Air factor
mix_ssd 	0 oven-dry weights, 1 SSD
mix_yield 	Yield
mix_notes 	Notes
