11.1 Sending a mix
PUT mixdesigns/ or mixdesigns/<mix_code> creates a mix that doesn't exist and
changes one that does. POST only creates. The body is the shape GET returns, inside a
mixdesigns array:
PUT /rhino_rest_api/v1/json/mixdesigns/4000EXT
{ "mixdesigns": [ { "mixdesign": {
"mixinfo": { "mix_code": "4000EXT", "mix_name": "4000 PSI Exterior",
"mix_price": 131.50,
"mix_slump": 5, "mix_mixtime": 1.5, "mix_air": 6,
"mix_notes": "air entrained" },
"mixcomponents": [
{ "mixcomponent": { "mc_code": "Sand", "mc_quantity": 1800 } },
{ "mixcomponent": { "mc_code": "Cement", "mc_quantity": 564 } },
{ "mixcomponent": { "mc_code": "Water", "mc_quantity": 32 } },
{ "mixcomponent": { "mc_code": "AEA", 	"mc_quantity": 22.5 } } ] } }
] }
