Concrete Rhino REST API Specification
Page 18 of 35

-- 18 of 35 --

Leave mixcomponents out to change only mixinfo . Send it and it is the whole design:
any component it doesn't list is removed from the mix. An empty list is refused (400).
A new mix needs mix_name and at least one component.
Changing mix_unittype needs mixcomponents in the same request, with the
amounts in the new units.
A mix can hold up to 24 components, each material once (400 otherwise). The same
mix twice in one request is refused (400).
A mix that is being batched right now returns 409. Try again when the load is done.
Loads queued for the mix stay.
A mix deleted at the plant isn't returned by GET, and a PUT or POST of its code returns
409.
Orders and loads stay attached to a renamed mix.
The reply is 201 Created if the request made at least one new mix, otherwise 201
Updated .
12. Orders
An order is found by its order number, order_num , which is the dispatch system's own
number for it. PUT creates an order that doesn't exist and updates one that does,
including PUT orders/<order_num> for a new number. POST only creates.
mixcomponent field 	Notes
mc_type 	Optional. If sent, it must be the material's
family (409 otherwise)
mc_mixcode 	Optional. If sent, it must be the mix's code,
old or new (400 otherwise)
mc_name , mc_source , mc_spgr ,
mc_absorption
Ignored. Change them with PUT materials/
