Setting an order to Complete or Canceled also removes its loads that haven't started and
parks the ones that have, the same as doing it on the order screen. Canceling also returns
the order's inventoried extras to inventory.
12.2 Reading orders
GET orders/ : open orders (status 1–5), soonest first by wanted time less travel time.
Orders with no wanted date come first.
GET orders/<date> or orders/<from>/<to> : orders wanted on those days, any
status, at most 93 days. A start after the end returns 400.
GET orders/<order_num> : one order, as a single "order": {...} .
orderslist/ in place of orders/ gives listitem records with order_num ,
status_id , qty_required and qty_remaining only.
An order as read can't be sent back unchanged: it carries the customer's name, not
cust_code .
