14.3 Removing a ticket
DELETE tickets/<ticket_num> removes the ticket if it hasn't started batching. It has no
body.
{
"request_status": { "status": 200, "msg": "OK", "detail": "Ok" },
"ticket": { "ticket_num": 100051, "order_num": "445676", "result":
"deleted" }
}
A ticket that has started batching or was canceled gets 409; an unknown ticket gets
404 Record not found.
The order and its billable extras are left as they are. Send the corrected order_qty
with the next ticket.
An order with no tickets left stays open. If the job is off, cancel it with orderstatus .
15. Loads and batch results
Loads are made at the plant, or sent by dispatch as tickets (section 14). The resources
here only read them. Two resources return them: loads in dispatch terms, and
batchresults in quality-control terms.
15.1 Loads
GET loads/ : every load that isn't canceled, oldest first. In this form order_num is "" .
GET loads/<date> or loads/<from>/<to> : loads made on those days, not canceled.
GET loads/<ticket> : the newest load with that ticket number, whatever its status, as
a one-element array. A ticket number can be reused once its load is finished, so older
loads with the number are history.
loadslist/ in place of loads/ gives short listitem records with no batched
weights, in an array named loadslist . This works with a date, a range or a ticket.
"Not canceled" means status below 6. A load the operator aborted and then finished
by hand counts as Complete.
{ "request_status": {...},
"loads": [ { "loads": {
"load": { "ticket": 100050, "order_num": "445676", ... },
"batchcomponents": [ { "batchcomponent": {...} } ] } } ] }
Concrete Rhino REST API Specification
Page 29 of 35

-- 29 of 35 --

Each array element is wrapped in "loads" , which holds the load's fields in "load" and
its batched weights in "batchcomponents" beside it. Under orderloads each element is
just {"load": {...}} , with no batchcomponents . A load whose truck, driver, customer
or order record was deleted is still returned, with those names blank.
Short listitem records carry plantcode , order_num , ticket , status , load_date ,
load_time , load_size and mix_code .
