15.2 Batch results
GET batchresults/<date> or batchresults/<from>/<to> : every load made on those
days that isn't canceled, including loads not batched yet (their bt_resultid is 0).
GET batchresults/<mix_code>/<from>/<to> : the same, for one mix.
GET batchresults/<ticket> : the newest load with that ticket number, as a single
"batchresult": {...} .
GET batchresults/ : every load on the computer that isn't canceled. This can be very
large; use a date range or result ids (section 15.3).
batchresultlist/ in place of batchresults/ gives short listitem records:
bt_ticket , bt_loaddate , bt_loadtime , bt_loadsize , bt_mixcode and
bt_resultid . It takes the same dates, mix and ticket codes; a ticket gives a one-
element array.
{ "request_status": {...},
"batchresults": [ { "batchresult": {
"batchinfo": { "bt_ticket": 100050, ... },
"batchcomponents": [ { "batchcomponent": {...} } ] } } ] }
batchcomponent field 	Meaning
bc_ticket 	Ticket number
bc_matcode , bc_mattype Material code and type (section 10)
bc_design 	Mix design amount
bc_target 	Target for this load
bc_actual 	Amount batched
bc_unit 	Unit code (section 11)
bc_freemoisture 	Free moisture %
batchinfo field 	Meaning
bt_ticket 	Ticket number
bt_plantcode 	This plant
