15.3 Collecting new batch results
Software that collects batch results should poll by result id rather than by date. Each
result then arrives once, in the order loads finished batching.
Result id. Each finished load has a result id, bt_resultid , in its batchinfo . Ids rise in
the order loads finish batching, so a load queued early but batched late gets a higher id
than loads that finished before it. A load that hasn't finished has 0.
Ping. GET status/ returns the plant's identity, clock and versions, and
newest_result_id . GET status/<result_id> also returns results_pending , the
number of results newer than that id.
New results. GET batchresults/since/<result_id> returns the finished results
newer than that id, oldest first, at most 100 per reply. "more" is always sent: 1 means
the page was full, so ask again from the last bt_resultid received. When nothing is
newer the reply is 204 with an empty array. Every result counted in results_pending
is returned, including loads whose truck, driver or order was later deleted.
batchresultlist/since/<result_id> returns short listitem records instead.
Many readers. The plant keeps no record of what has been read, so several programs
can poll one plant, each with its own last id. Polling doesn't affect a Universal Link
connection on the same plant.
batchinfo field 	Meaning
bt_mixcode 	Mix code
bt_custcode 	The customer's record id (a number, not
cust_code ); 0 if the customer record is gone
bt_jobcode 	Order number
bt_loaddate , bt_loadtime 	YYYY-MM-DD , HH:MM:SS
bt_loadsize 	Load size
bt_waterintruck 	Water in the truck
bt_watertrim 	The load's water adjustment
bt_batcher , bt_truck , bt_driver Who batched it, truck number, driver
bt_resultid 	Result id, for collecting new results (section 15.3); 0
if the load hasn't finished
Concrete Rhino REST API Specification
Page 32 of 35

-- 32 of 35 --

GET /rhino_rest_api/v1/json/status/2
{
"request_status": { "status": 200, "msg": "OK", "detail": "Ok" },
"status": { "plant_code": "101", "plant_name": "North Yard", "plant_time":
"2026-10-19 12:35:51",
"api_version": "v1", "software_version": "1.4.10.6",
"newest_result_id": 3, "results_pending": 1 }
}
A collecting program should:
1. Keep the highest bt_resultid it has received, starting at 0. Starting at 0 returns every
result on the plant computer, which can be a lot.
2. Call GET status/<last id> as often as it needs. When results_pending is above 0,
call GET batchresults/since/<last id> , store the results, and save the last
bt_resultid . Repeat while "more" is 1.
3. Once a day, also read the day by date ( batchresults/<date> ). A load finished by hand
on the load screen after an interruption keeps the result id of its last batch, which can
be older than results already received.
16. Limitations
Keys over plain HTTP. Over plain HTTP an API key can be read by anyone on the
network path. Use HTTPS or Tailscale for any connection that leaves the plant's local
network (section 4.1).
status field 	Meaning
plant_code , plant_name This plant
plant_time 	The plant computer's clock, YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS
local time
api_version 	v1
software_version 	The Concrete Rhino software version
newest_result_id 	Highest result id on the plant, 0 if none
results_pending 	Only with status/<result_id> : results newer
than that id
Concrete Rhino REST API Specification
Page 33 of 35

-- 33 of 35 --

HTTP status is always 200. The real result is in request_status.status . The
exception is a URL that doesn't have the API's form at all (such as
/rhino_rest_api/v1/json/ ), which gets the web server's own 404 page.
Codes containing / (such as 3/4 Rock ) can't go in a URL, even as %2F . Leave the
URL code off and send the code in the body.
Plants blank fields that aren't sent, and plant records are written one at a time without
a transaction (section 8).
cust_udf2 means discount on GET and price tier on PUT (section 9).
New orders get tax region 2, whatever the customer's region. Check tax on orders
created through the API.
Day-first dates can't be told from month-first ones (section 7). Send YYYY-MM-DD .
batchresults/ with no date returns every load on the computer. Use a date range or
result ids.
Plant computers not yet updated may answer a URL that ends in / with an empty
reply or 400 Unsupported format . Leave the trailing slash off for those plants.
Not available: DELETE of anything but a ticket, creating materials, projects, customer
search, and truck delivery times in batch results.
Tickets need a plant update made after 2026-10-19, and the behaviour in revision 2026-
10-20 needs one made after 2026-10-20. Older plants answer tickets/ with 404.
A ticket sent without ticket_num can't be changed or removed through the API. Send
a ticket number whenever dispatch has one.
